---
import { skills } from '../data/skills';
import SkillCard from './SkillCard.astro';
---

<section id="niche" aria-labelledby="niche-h" class="niche">
  <div class="heading-row">
    <div class="heading">
      <p class="eyebrow">02 / Approach</p>
      <h2 id="niche-h">Three skills<br />that travel.</h2>
    </div>
    <p class="intro">
      I learned this in sport, but the same pattern shows up in most industries. Specialists are
      buried in data, engineers need clear problems and leaders want a roadmap they can trust.
      I've been the user, the translator and the builder, which makes me quick at turning what
      people need into what gets built.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="cards">
    {skills.map((skill) => <SkillCard skill={skill} />)}
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .niche {
    max-width: var(--content-max);
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: var(--space-10) var(--space-5);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-7);
  }
  .heading-row {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(360px, 100%), 1fr));
    gap: 24px 64px;
    align-items: end;
  }
  .heading {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-4);
  }
  .eyebrow {
    margin: 0;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 13px;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }
  h2 {
    margin: 0;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 800;
    font-size: var(--text-section-h);
    line-height: 0.95;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }
  .intro {
    margin: 0;
    max-width: 520px;
    color: var(--color-ink-soft);
    text-wrap: pretty;
  }
  .cards {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(300px, 100%), 1fr));
    border-top: 2px solid var(--color-ink);
  }
</style>
